+   "Người Hy Lạp tin bầu trời phía trên mây chứa đầy Aether sáng trong.",
+   "Thứ không khí mà các vị thần hít thở.",
+   "Đầu óc con hôm nay trong trẻo như bầu trời trên cao."},
+  {"hemera", "Hemera",
+   "Nữ thần ban ngày, con của Erebus và Nyx.",
+   "Đem ánh sáng ban ngày đến mặt đất.",
+   "Ánh sáng ban ngày",
+   "Mỗi sáng Hemera rời nhà khi mẹ là Nyx trở về, hai mẹ con không bao giờ gặp nhau ở nhà.",
+   "Ban ngày, con gái của bóng đêm.",
+   "Một ngày tươi sáng nữa, nhờ có sách."},
+  {"tartarus", "Tartarus",
+   "Vực sâu nguyên thuỷ, sinh ra từ Chaos.",
+   "Giam giữ những kẻ thù của các thần.",
+   "Vực sâu · cánh cổng đồng",
+   "Một cái đe rơi chín ngày mới từ đất chạm tới đáy Tartarus.",
+   "Vực sâu đến mức cái đe rơi chín ngày mới chạm đáy.",
+   "Con đã đi sâu vào cuốn sách hơn bất cứ ai."},
+  {"pontus", "Pontus",
+   "Biển cả nguyên thuỷ, con của Gaia.",
+   "Là chính mặt biển, có trước cả Poseidon.",
+   "Sóng biển · cá",
+   "Pontus là cha của Nereus, ông già biển cả.",
+   "Biển cả có trước cả Poseidon.",
+   "Biển sách mênh mông, và con đang bơi rất giỏi."},
+  {"ananke", "Ananke",
+   "Nữ thần của tất yếu, có từ buổi đầu thế giới.",
+   "Ngay cả các vị thần cũng phải theo ý bà.",
+   "Trục quay · sợi chỉ",
+   "Ananke cầm trục quay của vũ trụ; các nữ thần Số Phận là con gái của bà.",
+   "Điều tất yếu mà cả thần cũng không cãi được.",
+   "Đọc mỗi ngày đã thành điều tất yếu của con."},
+  {"chronos", "Chronos",
+   "Thần thời gian nguyên thuỷ, khác với Titan Kronos.",
+   "Quay bánh xe của các mùa và năm tháng.",
+   "Bánh xe hoàng đạo · con rắn",
+   "Trong thơ Orpheus, Chronos là con rắn ba đầu ấp ra quả trứng vũ trụ.",
+   "Thời gian, đừng nhầm với vua Titan.",
+   "Thời gian con dành cho sách là thời gian không mất đi."},
+  {"metis", "Metis",
+   "Nữ Titan của trí khôn, con của Oceanus và Tethys.",
+   "Mưu trí và lời khuyên khôn ngoan.",
+   "Chén thuốc · con cú",
+   "Metis đưa Kronos chén thuốc làm ông nôn ra các con. Bà cũng là mẹ của Athena.",
+   "Mẹ của Athena, khôn ngoan nhất trong các Titan.",
+   "Một chút khôn ngoan mỗi ngày làm nên người khôn ngoan."},
+};
+
+constexpr Character ROSTER_EN[TOTAL_CHARACTERS] = {
+  {ROSTER[0].key, ROSTER[0].name,
+   "A winged horse, born from the blood of Medusa when Perseus cut off her head.",
+   "Flies as fast as the wind. Where his hoof strikes the ground, the spring of inspiration Hippocrene bursts out.",
+   "White wings · golden bridle",
+   "The hero Bellerophon tamed Pegasus with Athena's golden bridle, then rode him to defeat the monster Chimaera.",
+   "A white winged horse, born from the blood of a snake-haired monster.",
+   "Every page you read is a wingbeat. Look how high we're flying!"},
+  {ROSTER[1].key, ROSTER[1].name,
+   "A three-headed dog, child of Typhon and Echidna.",
+   "Guards the gate of the Underworld: lets the dead in, but lets no one out.",
+   "Three heads · serpent tail · gate of the Underworld",
+   "Heracles had to capture Cerberus alive in his last labour. Orpheus lulled him to sleep with music to slip past.",
+   "Three heads guarding a gate no one wants to reach.",
+   "All three of my heads want to hear the next chapter!"},
+  {ROSTER[2].key, ROSTER[2].name,
+   "The little owl who always perches on Athena's shoulder.",
+   "Sees clearly in the dark and notices what others miss.",
+   "Big eyes · olive branch · Athenian coin",
+   "The Athenians stamped Glaux on their silver coins. 'Bringing owls to Athens' means doing something needless.",
+   "Big eyes awake all night on the shoulder of the goddess of wisdom.",
+   "Hoo hoo! One more page, and you're a little wiser."},
+  {ROSTER[3].key, ROSTER[3].name,
+   "A tree nymph, born with a tree and living as long as it does.",
+   "Talks with the forest and makes trees sprout.",
+   "Oak leaves · wreath · tree trunk",
+   "When a Dryad's tree is cut down, she fades with it. That is why people of old asked permission before felling a tree.",
+   "A nymph who shares one life with a tree.",
+   "Books come from trees. When you read, the whole forest smiles."},
+  {ROSTER[4].key, ROSTER[4].name,
+   "A woodland spirit, half man and half goat, companion of Dionysus.",
+   "Plays the pipes, dances, and makes every party merrier.",
+   "Little horns · goat legs · pan pipes",
+   "The satyr Marsyas dared to challenge Apollo to a music contest and lost. After that, no one dared to compete with the god of music.",
+   "Horns, goat legs, and never without his pipes.",
+   "Done reading? Then let me play my pipes for you!"},
+  {ROSTER[5].key, ROSTER[5].name,
+   "A one-eyed giant, child of Ouranos and Gaia.",
+   "The finest metalsmith in the world.",
+   "One eye · smith's hammer · thunderbolt",
+   "The Cyclopes forged Zeus's thunderbolt, Poseidon's trident and Hades' helmet of invisibility.",
+   "One eye, one hammer, and Zeus's very first thunderbolt.",
+   "I only have one eye, and still I can see how hard you read."},
+  {ROSTER[6].key, ROSTER[6].name,
+   "The wisest and kindest centaur, son of the Titan Kronos.",
+   "Healing, archery and teaching.",
+   "Bow · healing herbs · Sagittarius constellation",
+   "Chiron taught Achilles, Jason and Asclepius. When he died, Zeus placed him among the stars.",
+   "Teacher of heroes, half man and half horse.",
+   "I once taught Achilles. You're teaching yourself just fine."},
+  {ROSTER[7].key, ROSTER[7].name,
+   "A creature with the body of a lion and the head and wings of an eagle.",
+   "Guards gold and treasure.",
+   "Claws · wings · gold",
+   "Old stories say Gryps built nests of gold in the northern mountains and drove off anyone who came to dig for it.",
+   "Half lion, half eagle, sleeping on a nest of gold.",
+   "I've guarded gold all my life, but your pages are worth more."},
+  {ROSTER[8].key, ROSTER[8].name,
+   "A many-headed water serpent from the swamp of Lerna.",
+   "Cut off one head and two grow back.",
+   "Nine heads · swamp",
+   "Heracles and his nephew Iolaus burned each neck after every cut so the Hydra's heads could not grow back.",
+   "Cut off one head and it grows two more.",
+   "You read one chapter, and I grow another head that wants more!"},
+  {ROSTER[9].key, ROSTER[9].name,
+   "A mixed monster: lion's head, goat's body, serpent's tail.",
+   "Breathes fire.",
+   "Three heads · flames",
+   "Bellerophon flew high on Pegasus and defeated the Chimaera without coming near its fire.",
+   "Lion, goat and snake in one body, and it breathes fire.",
+   "Lion head, goat head, snake tail: all three are full!"},
+  {ROSTER[10].key, ROSTER[10].name,
+   "A winged monster with a lion's body and a woman's head.",
+   "Asks riddles and devours anyone who answers wrong.",
+   "Riddle · wings · city of Thebes",
+   "Oedipus solved the riddle 'what walks on four legs in the morning, two at noon and three in the evening?'. The Sphinx lost and vanished.",
+   "Asks a riddle at the gate of Thebes.",
+   "Today's riddle: who reads every single day? You do!"},
+  {ROSTER[11].key, ROSTER[11].name,
+   "A monster with a bull's head and a man's body, from the island of Crete.",
+   "Terrible strength; lives in a labyrinth.",
+   "Bull horns · labyrinth · ball of thread",
+   "Theseus entered the labyrinth, slew the Minotaurus and found his way out thanks to Princess Ariadne's ball of thread.",
+   "Lives deep in a maze; only a ball of thread finds the way out.",
+   "No labyrinth gets me as lost as a good book."},
+  {ROSTER[12].key, ROSTER[12].name,
+   "One of the three Gorgon sisters, with snakes for hair.",
+   "Anyone who looks into her eyes turns to stone.",
+   "Snake hair · shield · stone statues",
+   "Perseus looked at Medusa only in his mirror-bright shield to cut off her head. Pegasus was born from her blood.",
+   "One look from her turns people to stone.",
+   "Don't look at me, look at the page. You won't turn to stone."},
+  {ROSTER[13].key, ROSTER[13].name,
+   "A bird monster with a human face, child of Thaumas and Electra.",
+   "Flies as fast as a storm wind and snatches other people's things.",
+   "Claws · whirlwind",
+   "The Harpies stole the food of the blind prophet Phineus until the heroes of the Argo chased them away.",
+   "Fast as a storm, always stealing someone's dinner.",
+   "I swooped in just to hear what you read today."},
+  {ROSTER[14].key, ROSTER[14].name,
+   "A bird maiden living on a rocky island at sea.",
+   "Her enchanting song lures sailors to steer onto the rocks.",
+   "Lyre · rocky island · song",
+   "Odysseus plugged his sailors' ears with wax and had himself tied to the mast so he could hear the song and live.",
+   "A song on a rocky island that pulls ships ashore.",
+   "My song is sweet, but your story is sweeter."},
+  {ROSTER[15].key, ROSTER[15].name,
+   "One of the fifty sea nymphs, daughters of the old sea god Nereus.",
+   "Helps sailors in trouble and calms the sea.",
+   "Seashell · dolphin · waves",
+   "Thetis, mother of Achilles, is the most famous Nereid. Her sisters often rode dolphins across the waves.",
+   "One of fifty sisters who live under the sea.",
+   "The sea is calm today, like the pages you just turned."},
+  {ROSTER[16].key, ROSTER[16].name,
+   "A nymph of springs, rivers and fresh-water wells.",
+   "Keeps the water clean and heals the sick.",
+   "Water jar · water lily · stream",
+   "Every spring has a Naiad to guard it. Some say their water gave poets inspiration.",
+   "A nymph in every spring and well.",
+   "My spring runs clear, and so does your mind after reading."},
+  {ROSTER[17].key, ROSTER[17].name,
+   "God of the countryside and shepherds, son of Hermes.",
+   "Plays the pipes and fills people with sudden fear.",
+   "Pan pipes · goat horns · meadow",
+   "Pan chased the nymph Syrinx; she turned into reeds. Pan cut the reeds into pipes and named them syrinx.",
+   "The shepherd god; the word 'panic' comes from his name.",
+   "Shh! The whole meadow went quiet so you could read."},
+  {ROSTER[18].key, ROSTER[18].name,
+   "The most talkative mountain nymph on Mount Kithairon.",
+   "Can only repeat the last words of others.",
+   "Cliff · echo",
+   "Hera punished Echo so she could only repeat what others said. She pined for Narcissus until only her voice was left.",
+   "Call out in the mountains and she answers with your own words.",
+   "Well read... well read... well read..."},
+  {ROSTER[19].key, ROSTER[19].name,
+   "A fire bird of the east; only one lives at a time.",
+   "Bursts into flame and is reborn from its own ashes.",
+   "Flames · ashes · egg of myrrh",
+   "Every five hundred years, the Phoenix builds a nest of myrrh, catches fire, and a young bird rises from the ashes.",
+   "Each time it dies, it rises again from the ashes.",
+   "Each book you finish, I'm reborn a little brighter."},
+  {ROSTER[20].key, ROSTER[20].name,
+   "A hundred-headed dragon guarding the golden apple tree in the garden of the Hesperides.",
+   "Never sleeps.",
+   "Golden apples · apple tree · dragon scales",
+   "Heracles needed three golden apples. Some say he slew Ladon; others say Atlas picked them for him.",
+   "Guards the golden apple tree at the western edge of the world.",
+   "I guard the golden apples. You guard your reading habit. Well done!"},
+  {ROSTER[21].key, ROSTER[21].name,
+   "A two-headed dog, brother of Cerberus.",
+   "Guards the red cattle of the giant Geryon.",
+   "Two heads · red cattle",
+   "In his tenth labour, Heracles struck Orthrus down with his club and drove Geryon's cattle away.",
+   "Brother of the three-headed dog, but with only two heads.",
+   "Both my heads agree: you read wonderfully today!"},
+  {ROSTER[22].key, ROSTER[22].name,
+   "A giant lion from the valley of Nemea.",
+   "Its hide cannot be pierced by any sword or spear.",
+   "Lion skin · Leo constellation",
+   "Heracles strangled the lion with his bare hands, then used its own claws to skin it and wore the hide as armour.",
+   "Heracles' first labour, with a hide tougher than any blade.",
+   "Nothing can pierce my hide, except a good story."},
+  {ROSTER[23].key, ROSTER[23].name,
+   "Son of Poseidon and Amphitrite, half man and half fish.",
+   "Blows his conch shell to raise the waves or calm the sea.",
+   "Conch shell · fish tail",
+   "After the great flood, Triton blew his conch to call the waters back from the land.",
+   "A fish tail and a conch shell the sea obeys.",
+   "I'll blow my conch and tell the whole sea: you read today!"},
+  {ROSTER[24].key, ROSTER[24].name,
+   "A six-headed sea monster living in a cave on a narrow strait.",
+   "Stretches her necks to snatch passing sailors.",
+   "Six heads · narrow strait",
+   "Odysseus had to sail close to Scylla or to the whirlpool Charybdis. He chose to lose six men rather than the whole ship.",
+   "Six heads waiting on one side of a narrow strait.",
+   "Six heads, six bellies, and every one of them is full!"},
+  {ROSTER[25].key, ROSTER[25].name,
+   "A hundred-eyed giant, Hera's faithful watchman.",
+   "Some of his eyes are always awake; nothing slips past him.",
+   "A hundred eyes · peacock tail",
+   "Hermes told stories until all hundred of Argus' eyes fell asleep. Hera set those eyes on the peacock's tail.",
+   "A hundred eyes that never all close at once.",
+   "All hundred of my eyes are following your page."},
+  {ROSTER[26].key, ROSTER[26].name,
+   "A giant of bronze forged by Hephaestus.",
+   "Walks around Crete three times a day to guard its shores.",
+   "Bronze body · nail in the heel",
+   "Talos' life ran through a single vein in his heel. The sorceress Medea pulled out the nail and Talos fell.",
+   "A bronze guard who walks around the island every day.",
+   "I'm made of bronze, but my heart warms each time you read."},
+  {ROSTER[27].key, ROSTER[27].name,
+   "A giant sea monster sent by Poseidon.",
+   "Raises the waves and swallows whole ships.",
+   "Cetus constellation · stormy waves",
+   "Cetus nearly swallowed Princess Andromeda, chained to a rock, but Perseus arrived in time to save her.",
+   "The sea monster that came for Princess Andromeda.",
+   "I'm as big as an island, and there's always room for one more chapter."},
+  {ROSTER[28].key, ROSTER[28].name,
+   "A sea horse: a horse in front, a fish tail behind.",
+   "Pulls Poseidon's chariot over the waves.",
+   "Fins · mane of foam · chariot",
+   "When Poseidon rides out, a team of Hippocampi pulls his chariot and the sea grows calm beneath the wheels.",
+   "The horse of the sea, pulling the sea king's chariot.",
+   "Hop on my back, I'll carry you to the next chapter!"},
+  {ROSTER[29].key, ROSTER[29].name,
+   "An immortal talking horse, child of Poseidon and Demeter.",
+   "The fastest of all horses.",
+   "Black mane · a neigh like a human voice",
+   "Arion carried the hero Adrastus out of the war of the Seven against Thebes when everyone else had fallen.",
+   "The fastest horse of all, and it can talk.",
+   "I'm the fastest horse alive, but I love reading slowly with you."},
+  {ROSTER[30].key, ROSTER[30].name,
+   "Youngest child of Kronos and Rhea, hidden in a cave on Crete so his father would not swallow him.",
+   "Hurls thunderbolts and rules the sky.",
+   "Thunderbolt · eagle · oak tree",
+   "Zeus grew up, freed his brothers and sisters from Kronos' belly, then led the gods to victory over the Titans.",
+   "King of the gods, holding a thunderbolt.",
+   "I give you the power of the thunderbolt: read fast, remember long."},
+  {ROSTER[31].key, ROSTER[31].name,
+   "Daughter of Kronos and Rhea, wife of Zeus.",
+   "Protects marriage and family.",
+   "Peacock · crown · pomegranate",
+   "Hera set the hundred eyes of Argus on the peacock's tail to remember her faithful watchman.",
+   "Queen of the gods. Her peacock carries a hundred eyes on its tail.",
+   "I keep a quiet corner for you. Read there every day."},
+  {ROSTER[32].key, ROSTER[32].name,
+   "Son of the Titans Kronos and Rhea, brother of Zeus. When the three brothers divided the world, he took the sea.",
+   "Calls up waves, shakes the earth, rides sea horses. Can make water flow from rock.",
+   "Trident · horse · dolphin · seashell",
+   "He competed with Athena to become patron of Athens. He offered a salty spring, Athena offered the olive tree, and the people chose Athena.",
+   "King of the sea, holding a trident.",
+   "Like the endless waves, every page you read carries you further."},
+  {ROSTER[33].key, ROSTER[33].name,
+   "Born from Zeus's head, already wearing armour.",
+   "Wisdom, strategy and crafts.",
+   "Owl · olive tree · Aegis shield",
+   "Athena beat Poseidon in the contest to protect Athens with her gift of the olive tree.",
+   "Born from her father's head in full armour.",
+   "Wisdom lights up every page you read. What you read today will stay with you."},
+  {ROSTER[34].key, ROSTER[34].name,
+   "Son of Zeus and Leto, born on the island of Delos.",
+   "Music, poetry, light and prophecy.",
+   "Lyre · laurel wreath · sun",
+   "Apollo founded his oracle at Delphi after slaying the serpent Python.",
+   "God of song, crowned with laurel.",
+   "Every word is a note. Today you added another song."},
+  {ROSTER[35].key, ROSTER[35].name,
+   "Twin sister of Apollo, daughter of Zeus and Leto.",
+   "Hunting, the wild and the moon.",
+   "Silver bow · deer · crescent moon",
+   "As a child, Artemis asked Zeus to let her stay free forever and to give her a silver bow, and Zeus agreed.",
+   "A huntress with a silver bow under the moon.",
+   "Like a silver arrow, you hit your target today."},
+  {ROSTER[36].key, ROSTER[36].name,
+   "Daughter of Kronos and Rhea, mother of Persephone.",
+   "Harvest, wheat and fertile land.",
+   "Sheaf of wheat · torch · sickle",
+   "When Hades took Persephone away, Demeter grieved so much that plants stopped growing. That was the first winter.",
+   "Goddess of wheat, whose sorrow made winter.",
+   "The seeds you sow each day will become a harvest."},
+  {ROSTER[37].key, ROSTER[37].name,
+   "Son of Zeus and Hera.",
+   "Strength and courage in battle.",
+   "War helmet · spear · hunting dog",
+   "Ares was hot-headed. He lost to Athena twice because she kept a cooler head.",
+   "God of war in a bronze helmet.",
+   "You defeated laziness today. I respect that."},
+  {ROSTER[38].key, ROSTER[38].name,
+   "Born from the sea foam near the island of Cyprus.",
+   "Love and beauty.",
+   "Dove · rose · seashell",
+   "Paris gave the golden apple to Aphrodite as the most beautiful. That gift led to the Trojan War.",
+   "Born from the sea foam, winner of the golden apple.",
+   "Love your books like an old friend."},
+  {ROSTER[39].key, ROSTER[39].name,
+   "Son of Zeus and the nymph Maia. On the day he was born he stole Apollo's cattle.",
+   "Carries messages, runs fast, guides souls.",
+   "Winged sandals · snake staff · winged hat",
+   "Hermes made the first lyre from a tortoise shell and gave it to Apollo to say sorry for the cattle.",
+   "A messenger in winged sandals who stole cattle on his very first day.",
+   "My winged sandals will carry you to the next chapter."},
+  {ROSTER[40].key, ROSTER[40].name,
+   "Son of Hera, blacksmith of the gods.",
+   "Forges weapons and wondrous objects.",
+   "Hammer · anvil · forge",
+   "Hephaestus forged Achilles' armour, the chariot of Helios and the bronze giant Talos.",
+   "Blacksmith of Olympus, who even made a man of bronze.",
+   "Every page is a hammer blow. You are forging yourself."},
+  {ROSTER[41].key, ROSTER[41].name,
+   "Son of Zeus and Princess Semele, born a second time from Zeus's thigh.",
+   "Wine, festivals and theatre.",
+   "Grapes · thyrsus staff · leopard",
+   "The first Greek plays were performed at festivals in honour of Dionysus.",
+   "God of festivals, born twice.",
+   "You had a reading day worth celebrating. Be merry!"},
+  {ROSTER[42].key, ROSTER[42].name,
+   "Eldest brother of Zeus, who took the Underworld when the world was divided.",
+   "Rules the dead and the treasures beneath the earth.",
+   "Helmet of invisibility · Cerberus · sceptre",
+   "Hades took Persephone to the Underworld. Because she ate six pomegranate seeds, she must stay six months every year.",
+   "King of the world below, with a helmet of invisibility.",
+   "Real treasure lies deep below. You dug up a little more today."},
+  {ROSTER[43].key, ROSTER[43].name,
+   "Eldest child of Kronos and Rhea.",
+   "Keeps the fire burning in every home.",
+   "Hearth · kettle",
+   "Hestia gave up her seat on Olympus to Dionysus so she could tend the central fire.",
+   "The gentlest goddess, sitting by the hearth.",
+   "A small fire each day keeps the whole house warm. Don't let it go out."},
+  {ROSTER[44].key, ROSTER[44].name,
+   "Daughter of Zeus and Demeter, queen of the Underworld.",
+   "Brings spring back every year.",
+   "Pomegranate · flowers · torch",
+   "Every time Persephone returns from the Underworld to her mother, the earth bursts into bloom.",
+   "Six pomegranate seeds keep her in the world below.",
+   "After every winter comes spring. The next chapter will be brighter."},
+  {ROSTER[45].key, ROSTER[45].name,
+   "A goddess of Titan blood whom Zeus still honoured.",
+   "Magic, crossroads and torchlight in the night.",
+   "Two torches · key · black dog",
+   "Hecate carried torches to help Demeter search for her daughter in the night.",
+   "Stands at the crossroads holding two torches.",
+   "At every crossroads, my torch shows you the way with books."},
+  {ROSTER[46].key, ROSTER[46].name,
+   "Son of Aphrodite.",
+   "Shoots arrows that make people fall in love.",
+   "Bow and arrows · wings",
+   "Eros accidentally pricked himself and fell in love with Psyche. After many trials, Psyche became a goddess.",
+   "A winged boy with arrows of love.",
+   "My arrow has hit you: you will love this book."},
+  {ROSTER[47].key, ROSTER[47].name,
+   "Daughter of the Titan Pallas and Styx.",
+   "Brings victory to those who deserve it.",
+   "Wings · laurel wreath · palm branch",
+   "Nike stood in the hand of Athena's statue in the Parthenon, ready to hand out the victor's wreath.",
+   "A winged goddess who crowns the winner.",
+   "Another day of victory. This laurel wreath is yours."},
+  {ROSTER[48].key, ROSTER[48].name,
+   "Daughter of Thaumas and Electra, sister of the Harpies.",
+   "Carries messages between heaven and earth along the rainbow.",
+   "Rainbow · water jug · wings",
